# No trailing slash, deliberately.
#
# `node_modules/` matches a DIRECTORY called node_modules and nothing else. A
# symlink called node_modules — which is what a linked local dependency is, and
# what several package managers create — is not a directory, so the pattern
# misses it and the link gets committed. That has happened on this codebase
# once already: a symlink pointing at its own parent went into a commit, and
# every checkout afterwards failed with ELOOP.
node_modules

# The build. Nothing serves it — `run.sh` runs Vite — and a checked-in copy is a
# second answer to "what does this page say", which disagrees with the first the
# moment somebody edits `page/`. Three separate afternoons on this codebase were
# spent on a stale `dist` answering 200.
dist

# This app's own store: every notification it has been shown. Unlike the other
# modules here there is no `seed/` beside it and there must not be — a
# notification panel that shipped with notifications in it would be a program
# telling somebody things happened on their machine that did not. An empty first
# screen is the true one, and the page says so in words.
data
